WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.680
David Tennant is one of the most beloved actors&nbsp;
around, with acclaimed turns as The Doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:11.600
and Detective Alec Hardy on "Broadchurch." So&nbsp;
why haven't you heard from him lately? It isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.240
like he's stopped working. He has stayed pretty&nbsp;
busy, but with projects you may not have seen.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:22.720
Don't get us wrong, we're not here to judge. In&nbsp;
fact, if the only TV show you regularly watch or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.360
pay attention to is "Doctor Who," you might&nbsp;
be doing something right. Launched in 1963,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.280
the ongoing adventure of the time and&nbsp;
space-traveling do-gooder known as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:37.360
Doctor remains an intensely influential sci-fi&nbsp;
institution. In part, this is by virtue of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:42.880
having existed for so long. If a person feels like&nbsp;
watching "Doctor Who" and absolutely nothing else,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:47.200
that person could certainly manage that&nbsp;
without boredom ever presenting itself as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.040
a major problem. Tennant's three seasons&nbsp;
alone could tide one over for a while.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:56.480
Tennant's Tenth Doctor appears in at least two&nbsp;
of the best "Doctor Who" episodes of all time:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:02.240
"Blink" and "The Girl In The Fireplace." His&nbsp;
run didn't just wow fans — it reinvigorated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:06.880
"Doctor Who" as a whole. So if this is&nbsp;
still what you know Tennant best for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.800
well, you've got taste. But if it&nbsp;
is, in fact, your preference to watch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:14.960
nothing except "Doctor Who," it explains why&nbsp;
you haven't heard from the man in a while,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:19.520
as he hasn't regularly been on that&nbsp;
show since President Obama's first term.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:20.468
"Don't be ridiculous."

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.680
We should clarify that when we&nbsp;
say David Tennant does not appear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:31.200
regularly on "Doctor Who," we're referring to the&nbsp;
BBC television program. But while his time as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:37.280
physical presence on the TARDIS ended in 2010,&nbsp;
his time as the Doctor continues to this day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:42.320
The Tenth Doctor joins forces with Tom Baker's&nbsp;
indispensable Fourth Doctor, with their original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:47.920
actors voicing both characters, in the audio&nbsp;
drama "Out Of Time," released in August 2020.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:54.320
This is enormously exciting for fans: The Fourth&nbsp;
Doctor, who Baker portrayed from 1974 to 1981,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.320
still stands as one of the most&nbsp;
widely-recognized versions of the character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:02.240
But this production is actually not all&nbsp;
that out of the ordinary for Tennant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:05.360
who records Doctor Who audio dramas all the time.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:10.240
In fact, it just so happens that "Doctor&nbsp;
Who" related projects only comprise a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:15.680
fraction of Tennant's extensive audio drama&nbsp;
and audio book catalog. His participation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:22.160
in audio "Who" actually dates back to before&nbsp;
Christopher Eccleston rebooted the role in 2005:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:26.560
Tennant played a non-leading part&nbsp;
in 2001's "Doctor Who: Colditz,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:32.160
a story involving Nazis who somehow gain access&nbsp;
to the TARDIS at the conclusion of World War II.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:38.000
"Doctor Who" has not yet produced a video game&nbsp;
major crossover success just yet. But just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:43.360
like James Bond, Marvel Comics, and other major&nbsp;
franchises with similar longevity, the beloved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:48.400
series has been churning out video games for&nbsp;
pretty much as long as video games have existed.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:53.040
This brings us to "Doctor Who: The Edge&nbsp;
of Reality." The game's official website&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:58.160
describes "Edge of Reality" as a reimagining&nbsp;
of 2019's "Doctor Who: The Edge of Time,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.960
a VR game for console and PC. Where "Edge of&nbsp;
Time" features the Thirteenth Doctor played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:08.240
by Jodie Whittaker, "Reality" includes both&nbsp;
her and David Tennant as the Tenth Doctor.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:12.160
According to the game's official website,&nbsp;
Edge of Reality will see the Doctors address&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.360
a threat to all of reality. It pits the&nbsp;
player against Daleks, Weeping Angels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:22.240
Cybermen, and various lesser-known but&nbsp;
equally-deadly intergalactic baddies.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.400
As far as Tennant goes, it's basically&nbsp;
a continuation of his already extensive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:30.080
catalogue of Who-related voiceover&nbsp;
work. But the jump from audio books&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:34.720
to games is significant for his fans —&nbsp;
you can't play an audio book, after all.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:39.040
"You need my voice in particular.&nbsp;
The cleverest voice in the room."

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.840
Everybody's got a podcast these days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:46.000
including our man David Tennant. His&nbsp;
podcast, featuring the uninspiring name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:52.160
"David Tennant Does A Podcast With…" began in&nbsp;
2019 and has been running every week since.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:55.920
This series of hour-long conversations&nbsp;
with Tennant's fellow famous people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.520
is a delightful project for&nbsp;
Tennant fans of all stripes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:05.040
Notable guests include US politician and&nbsp;
activist Stacey Abrams, author Neil Gaiman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:10.000
actress Elisabeth Moss, former "Doctor&nbsp;
Who" star Billie Piper, and many others.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.240
Unsurprisingly, Tennant's got a knack&nbsp;
for cultivating engaging discourse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:17.840
"David Tennant Does A Podcast With…"&nbsp;
plays out in roughly the same playful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:23.680
spirit as Marc Maron's "WTF:" the host&nbsp;
and guest take a seemingly unscripted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:29.440
casual journey through the latter's life, career,&nbsp;
ideas, attitudes, and anecdotes, plus any other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:34.880
subjects they stumble into. Tennant hasn't been&nbsp;
in the podcasting game for as long as Maron, or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:39.520
many other well-known podcast hosts with a&nbsp;
similar sensibility. But Tennant makes up for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:45.360
his lack of experience with his easygoing nature,&nbsp;
disarming charm, and engaging Scottish accent.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:51.280
By no means did David Tennant drop off of&nbsp;
television after "Doctor Who." In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:56.560
for certain demographics, Doctor Who might not&nbsp;
even be the program for which he's most famous.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:59.120
David Tennant voiced the lead role on "DuckTales,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:02.800
a celebrated reboot of the&nbsp;
1987 cartoon of the same name.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:06.640
If you've seen "DuckTales" in its modern&nbsp;
incarnation and didn't recognize David&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:09.360
Tennant, you don't need to feel like a dumb-dumb:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:12.880
he appears in the role of the&nbsp;
billionaire mallard Scrooge McDuck.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:17.520
The reboot has been met with an abundance&nbsp;
of praise – a major feat in any case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.800
but especially impressive when&nbsp;
one considers the fact that people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:25.200
love the '80s "DuckTales" series. At the risk&nbsp;
of blasphemy, we're going to go ahead and say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:30.320
the new DuckTales doesn't just earn that praise&nbsp;
... it might surpass the original cartoon. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:35.200
humor and storytelling can keep adults in the&nbsp;
room interested without alienating any kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:40.240
the cast is star-studded, and, most importantly,&nbsp;
Huey, Dewey, and Louie don't emulate their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:44.480
Uncle Donald's unintelligible squawking.&nbsp;
Instead, Donald's nephews sound like the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:48.960
famous comedians who do their voices.&nbsp;
That is a seriously major improvement.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:53.400
"I promise I won't let anything bad happen to ya."

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:02.880
The miniseries "Good Omens," starring the one&nbsp;
and only David Tennant, burst onto Amazon Prime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:08.880
in May of 2019. Based on the 1990 Neil Gaiman&nbsp;
and Terry Pratchett novel of the same name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:14.240
"Good Omens" involves a demon played by Tennant,&nbsp;
an angel played by Michael Sheen, their unlikely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:19.920
friendship, and various factors pertaining to the&nbsp;
biblical end of all life in the universe. The cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:25.440
also includes John Hamm, Miranda Richardson,&nbsp;
and Frances McDormand, who portrays God.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:30.560
While "Good Omens" is not as culturally prevalent&nbsp;
as some of Tennant's other work, it was a slam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:35.360
dunk in terms of quality: Critics almost all&nbsp;
got a real kick out of it. Meanwhile, author&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:41.280
Neil Gaiman has said he found the experience of&nbsp;
making the series wildly educational, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:46.160
in regards to his professional transition from&nbsp;
full-time wordsmith to television showrunner.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.560
In a roundabout way, that means we have&nbsp;
David Tennant to thank for whatever success&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:55.280
is enjoyed by Netflix's "Sandman" series, on&nbsp;
which Gaiman serves as executive producer.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:00.720
During the COVID-19 pandemic, people discovered&nbsp;
all kinds of awesome activities you can do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:04.880
without going outside. You can watch movies.&nbsp;
You can watch television. You can read books.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:10.080
You can play board games ... and that's pretty&nbsp;
much everything. As for things you can't do?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:13.760
Well, you can't film a television series&nbsp;
about traveling the circumference of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:16.240
world in a hot-air balloon.&nbsp;
If that's your objective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:21.920
you're going to have to wait until the pandemic&nbsp;
is over, or at least has subsided significantly.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:25.520
The eight-episode limited series&nbsp;
"Around The World in 80 Days" took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:30.880
a pandemic-mandated production pause back in&nbsp;
March 2020 and resumed shooting in November.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:36.720
This TV adaptation of the 1872 novel by&nbsp;
Jules Verne stars Tennant as Phileas Fogg,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:42.560
the gambling protagonist, appearing alongside&nbsp;
Leonie Benesch as Detective Fix and Ibrahim Koma&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:47.520
as Passepartout. It looks to be a whimsical&nbsp;
and exciting updating of the classic story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:52.880
and the talent in the main ensemble is&nbsp;
seriously impressive. It releases in late 2021.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:57.280
There's a pretty significant problem with&nbsp;
our collective preoccupation with major&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:01.120
streaming platforms. Namely, if anything&nbsp;
cool or interesting comes out on one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:05.200
the lesser-known services, we might not&nbsp;
find out about it until months later.

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:09.840
So if you didn't notice David Tennant's&nbsp;
turn as convicted serial killer and really,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:15.520
really creepy dude Dennis Nilsen, we can't&nbsp;
blame you: the three-part 2020 series "Des"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:19.680
is available on the little-known platform&nbsp;
Sundance Now. It's well worth seeking out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:24.720
however, even if it does mean signing up for yet&nbsp;
another streaming service. The searing drama got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:29.280
some pretty positive feedback, with Tennant's&nbsp;
performance praised as his most unsettling and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:34.240
upsetting to date. Keep in mind, one of Tennant's&nbsp;
most famous roles happens to be Kilgrave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:39.120
a homicidal abuser with mind-control powers.&nbsp;
Still, the critics urge us to believe that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:44.880
next to his depiction of Nilsen, Kilgrave comes&nbsp;
off as well-adjusted and socially acceptable.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:48.960
We shouldn't define Tennant's career, or&nbsp;
even judge his artistic instincts, based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:55.040
on a handful of roles cherry-picked off a CV that&nbsp;
has been steadily expanding since 1988, of course.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.680
But it is a pretty funny coincidence that&nbsp;
we recognize him primarily as either a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:03.920
happy-go-lucky fantasy character like&nbsp;
the Doctor or Scrooge McDuck ... or as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:08.720
homicidal sociopath like Nilsen or Kilgrave.&nbsp;
The public seems to prefer David Tennant as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:12.960
one extreme or the other – and it seems he&nbsp;
likes taking those over-the-top roles, too.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:18.640
The Coronavirus pandemic had a disastrous effect&nbsp;
on every industry, including the entertainment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:22.640
industry. Massive delays were put on several&nbsp;
productions in order to help stop the spread&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:27.920
of the disease, and it was a difficult situation&nbsp;
to try to adapt to and film around. Thus, it isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:32.960
exactly surprising that we didn't get a ton of&nbsp;
notable pandemic films or TV shows either — but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:39.280
a few did make it out of creative brains and into&nbsp;
existence. "Staged" is a perfect example of this.

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:44.160
"Staged" stars David Tennant and his "Good&nbsp;
Omens" co-star Michael Sheen as exaggerated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:48.560
versions of themselves. That's right: this is&nbsp;
one of those fictionalized-real-people affairs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.920
a la Keanu Reeves in "Always Be My Maybe."

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:59.520
"It's called Vice Breaker. It's like truth&nbsp;
or dare, but a little more apocalyptic."

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:04.400
In "Staged," Tennant and Sheen are set to star in&nbsp;
a production of "Six Characters in Search of an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:09.280
Author" by Luigi Pirandello, but the production&nbsp;
faces an indefinite delay due to the pandemic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:14.080
lockdown of pretty much every stage in Europe.&nbsp;
The pair of actors decide to rehearse and cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:19.600
the play over Zoom. As viewing experiences go,&nbsp;
Staged resonates like a digital, British version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:24.240
of "Curb Your Enthusiasm." Check it out, and we'd&nbsp;
encourage you to go in without doing too much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:28.640
reading about it: there are some incredible&nbsp;
guest appearances that are great surprises.

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:33.360
The disappointing fate of Marvel's first attempt&nbsp;
at putting the Marvel Cinematic Universe on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:38.640
streaming television has been well documented.&nbsp;
As a result, it's easy to forget there was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:44.560
time when Kevin Feige would've been crazy to act&nbsp;
like Netflix's Marvel output didn't count as canon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:49.040
MCU material. The first season of "Jessica&nbsp;
Jones" was particularly well received, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:54.720
Tennant deserves significant credit for this turn&nbsp;
of events. Let us not forget that back in 2015,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.720 --> 00:11:00.320
the only MCU villains anyone considered worth a&nbsp;
darn were Loki, fellow Netflix baddie Wilson Fisk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:04.480
and Tennant's Kilgrave, oft-referred&nbsp;
to in the comics as the Purple Man.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:08.880
As Kilgrave, Tennant inverts the quirky&nbsp;
charm he wields as the Doctor and stuffs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:14.000
it into a sociopath that Jessica Jones combats&nbsp;
throughout the latter two-thirds of the season.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:18.240
Kilgrave ceases to be a series regular&nbsp;
following the initial 13 episodes, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:22.160
and while we'd like to make a case that&nbsp;
Kilgrave's exit doesn't serve the show's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:26.400
larger story and other characters, we can't.&nbsp;
Despite the quality of Tennant's performance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:30.480
"Jessica Jones" made the right call in&nbsp;
keeping Kilgrave out of its second season.

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:35.040
But, in an alternate-universe scenario where the&nbsp;
folks in charge of the MCU decided to do more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:40.480
stuff with Kilgrave, Marvel fans would probably&nbsp;
be talking about David Tennant more often. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:44.880
we've seen comic book characters come back from&nbsp;
worse, so we've still got our fingers crossed!

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:47.760
Check out one of our newest&nbsp;
videos right here! Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:50.800
even more Looper videos about your&nbsp;
favorite stars are coming soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:55.840
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit&nbsp;
the bell so you don't miss a single one.

